			"Message": "feat(Grove): Initialize Rust/WASM extension host scaffold\n\nIntroduces `Grove`, a new Element within the Land ecosystem designed to host high-performance Rust and WebAssembly VS Code extensions. This component complements the Node.js-based `Cocoon` host by providing a secure, sandboxed execution environment using Wasmtime.\n\nKey infrastructure changes include:\n- **Cargo Configuration**: Defines `Cargo.toml` with dependencies on `wasmtime`, `tokio`, and `tonic` (gRPC) to support async WASM execution and communication with the `Mountain` backend.\n- **Build System**: Implements `build.rs` to conditionally compile Protocol Buffer definitions (`Grove.proto`) for native builds and configure linker flags for `wasm32-wasi` targets.\n- **Tooling**: Adds `.cargo/config.toml` to manage target-specific `rustflags` for Apple Silicon (x86_64/aarch64) and WASM stack sizing.\n- **Documentation**: Provides a comprehensive `README.md` outlining the architecture, module structure (Host, WASM Runtime, Transport Layer), and integration points with `Mountain` via the `Vine` protocol.\n\nThis scaffold establishes the necessary project structure to bridge the Land extension API with native/WASM runtimes.",
